course: dictionary
lesson: 5916
title: Marmite and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of real things, and some have a second meaning when people talk informally. Marmite is both. It is a brand name for a dark brown, sticky, salty spread, eaten on toast, especially in the UK. «In Sydney, Ethan-Jay's grandparents post Cadbury chocolate and Marmite from England.» The sentence tells you Marmite is a food that comes from England.
explain: Context helps with the second meaning. «His mates go, "Ew, Marmite?", and he eats it anyway.» The "Ew" shows his mates do not like it, and "he eats it anyway" shows he does not mind. So "a Marmite thing" means something people either love or hate, with nobody in the middle.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does "a Marmite thing" still make sense if you say "a thing people love or hate"? Yes, so you have it right. When you are unsure, look the word up in a dictionary, and remember that a dictionary tells you which meaning is the everyday one and which is slang.
fact: Marmite is a dark brown, sticky, salty spread, eaten on toast, especially in the UK.
fact: New Zealand has its own Marmite too, and Australians have a similar spread called Vegemite.
fact: Informal, UK: "a Marmite thing" means something people either love or hate, with nobody in the middle.
fact: Marmite is made from yeast left over from brewing beer, and it contains B vitamins.
fact: In French, «une marmite» means a large cooking pot, and that is the picture shown on the jar.
exercise: What is Marmite? | *A dark brown, sticky, salty spread made from yeast | A sweet red jam made from strawberries | A large cooking pot for soup | A fizzy drink from Australia
exercise: Ethan-Jay's mates say «Ew, Marmite?» and he eats it anyway. What does "a Marmite thing" mean? | A thing made in a large pot | *Something people either love or hate, with nobody in the middle | Something kept in a jar on a shelf | Something everybody loves
exercise: The jar shows the French words «une marmite». What do they mean in English? | Toast with butter | A brown sauce for chips | *A large cooking pot | A fizzy drink
test: In «his mates go, "Ew, Marmite?"», what does "Ew" show? | *Dislike, a feeling of yuck | Hunger before lunch | Surprise at the price | Delight at a birthday treat
test: Why does Ethan-Jay eat the Marmite? | Because his mates dared him to try it | *He likes it anyway, even though his mates say ew | Because it is chocolate | Because he is cooking a meal
exam: Which phrase means something people either love or hate, with nobody in the middle? | *A Marmite thing | Toast crumbs | An Aussie thing | A jam jar
